Quay robot tokens do not span Some users however do want to pull across organizations using robot OpenShift permits multiple namespaces to be provided within a `dockerconfigjson` secret so this can theoretically be done via a single service For example:
{code:java}
{
 "auths": {
 "quay.io/org1":
{ "auth": "super secret", "email": "" }
,
 "quay.io/org2":
{ "auth": "even more secret", "email": "" }
,
 "quay.io/org3":
{ "auth": "oh-la-la-dont-look", "email": "" }
 }
 }
{code}
The single SA can then be used across Kube namespaces as needed to overcome the token scoping Docs should reflect this technique as a workaround for robot token scoping within a single namespace.
See comment below for email thread discussion.

