When following the documentation here:
[
This command results in an error:
{code:java}
docker run --restart on-failure \
 -e SERVER=ws://myquayenterprise \
 -v /mnt/docker.sock:/mnt/docker.sock \
 quay.io/redhat/quay-builder:v3.0.3
{code}
The error is only found when attempting a build:
{code:java}
build resulted in an error: dial unix /var/run/docker.sock: connect: no such file or directory
{code}
The command should be this on Red Hat Enterprise Linux: (The 'Z' option adds the appropriate SELinux labels)
{code:java}
docker run --restart on-failure \ 
 -e SERVER=ws://myquayenterprise \ 
 -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock:Z \ 
 quay.io/redhat/quay-builder:v3.0.3
{code}

Under section 
Run the build worker image
Replace: 
{code:java}
docker run --restart on-failure -e SERVER=wss://myquayenterprise -v /path/to/ssl/rootCA.pem:/usr/local/share/ca-certificates/rootCA.pem -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock --entrypoint /bin/sh quay.io/coreos/quay-builder:v2.9.3 -c '/usr/sbin/update-ca-certificates && quay-builder'
{code}
With:
{code:java}
docker run --restart on-failure -e SERVER=wss://myquayenterprise -v /path/to/ssl/rootCA.pem:/certs/rootCA.pem -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock quay.io/coreos/quay-builder:v2.9.3
{code}
Thus, the setup is simplified! old way still works for Alpine based Quay builder image, but the new way works for both rhel and alpine based image!

